<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  A TEMPLATE, not a loadable job. Every {ROOT} below is a placeholder.

  Render it with the project folder written in, and it becomes a plist launchd
  will accept. From the project folder:

    sed "s|{ROOT}|$PWD|g" config/launchd/templates/sheet_sync.plist.tmpl \
      > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.mtalib.agentic-trading.sheet_sync.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) \
      ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.mtalib.agentic-trading.sheet_sync.plist

  WHY THIS ONE IS NOT GENERATED LIKE THE SIX LIVE JOBS. Those are written by
  scripts/gen_launchd.py from config/launchd/templates/, and
  this file is skipped there because it is a finished plist and not a template
  in that folder's own format, whatever its name suggests. gen_launchd.py names
  it out loud on every run rather than passing over it in silence. Also,
  tests/test_paths.py checks that every generated plist matches its template and
  that each job wakes up exactly the number of times it is meant to. This job
  has never run against the real sheet, so it is deliberately kept out of that
  set, exactly like deadman.plist.tmpl beside it. Adding it would put an
  unwatched job into the same list as the ones that are ready.

  When Mo decides to arm it, the move is small and worth doing properly:

    1. write config/launchd/templates/sheet_sync.template in gen_launchd's own
       format, with the program, environment and comment from this file, and the
       schedule line reading exactly:
         at 16:35 on weekdays
    2. add "sheet_sync": 5 to EXPECTED_WAKE_UPS in tests/test_paths.py
    3. run scripts/gen_launchd.py to write the plist, then run it again with the
       install flag to load it

  WHAT IT DOES. At 16:35 New York, Monday to Friday, thirty five minutes after
  the market shuts, it rewrites the Google Sheet ledger from the database. The
  database is the record; the sheet is a picture of it that Mo can open on a
  phone. Nothing writes to the sheet during the day any more, so a broken wifi
  connection at half past nine in the morning costs nothing.

  IT CANNOT TRADE. It reads one file on disk and writes to one Google Sheet. It
  never opens a connection to IB Gateway and has no way to place an order.

  IT IS SAFE TO RUN TWICE. Every tab is cleared over the columns the agent owns
  and rewritten from the top, so a second run in the same evening produces the
  same sheet rather than a doubled one.

  TAKE THE LAST ARGUMENT OUT of ProgramArguments below, the write flag, and it
  becomes a rehearsal: it works out every row, reads the live sheet to check the
  column headings still line up, prints what it would send, and writes nothing.
  That is the way to watch it for a week before trusting it. (The flag cannot be
  spelled out here, because XML forbids two hyphens in a row inside a comment.)

  WHAT IT NEEDS. The Google token at .secrets/token_personal_drive.json and the
  sheet id in config/ledger.json. If either is missing it says so and stops
  without touching anything.

  launchd works in this Mac's own local time. There is no setting in here that
  pins a time zone, so the time below is this Mac's clock. The market keeps New
  York hours whatever the Mac thinks. Keep the Mac on Eastern, or change the
  time in here.

  NOT LOADED by writing this file. Loading is the separate, deliberate step
  written out above.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.mtalib.agentic-trading.sheet_sync</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
      <string>{ROOT}/venv312/bin/python</string>
      <string>{ROOT}/ledger/sync_sheet.py</string>
      <string>--write</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>{ROOT}</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>{ROOT}/output/launchd_sheet_sync.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>{ROOT}/output/launchd_sheet_sync.err.log</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
      <key>AGENTIC_TRADING_ROOT</key><string>{ROOT}</string>
      <key>PATH</key><string>/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin</string>
      <key>TZ</key><string>America/New_York</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- A run that overruns must never have a second one land on top of it. A
         whole month of rows is a handful of requests to Google, so a few
         minutes is generous and it only runs once a day anyway. -->
    <key>AbandonProcessGroup</key>
    <false/>
    <key>ExitTimeOut</key>
    <integer>300</integer>

    <!-- Do not fire the moment the job is loaded, only at 16:35. A job that
         fired at load would rewrite the sheet in the middle of a trading
         morning from a database that is only half way through the day. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <!-- 5 wake ups a week: 16:35, Monday to Friday. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
      <dict>
        <key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer>
        <key>Hour</key><integer>16</integer>
        <key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>Weekday</key><integer>2</integer>
        <key>Hour</key><integer>16</integer>
        <key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>Weekday</key><integer>3</integer>
        <key>Hour</key><integer>16</integer>
        <key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>Weekday</key><integer>4</integer>
        <key>Hour</key><integer>16</integer>
        <key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>Weekday</key><integer>5</integer>
        <key>Hour</key><integer>16</integer>
        <key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer>
      </dict>
    </array>

</dict>
</plist>
